Imagine you’re baking a cake. 🎂 First, you need a recipe (your program). Then you gather ingredients (data like radius), mix them (calculate area), and finally serve the cake (display the result).

A Java program works the same way:
• It starts with a class (like a recipe book)
• Has a main method (the actual recipe)
• Uses variables to hold data (your ingredients)

Here’s the simplest structure:
```java
public class ComputeArea {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Your code goes here
    }
}
```
Think of `main` as the starting line of a race - this is where your program begins running!

